From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: preload seven pixels in QSEED4 behind the inline
 rotator

With true inline rotation (patch 0066) the rotator output feeds the QSEED4
scaler, which is programmed with the default horizontal preload of 4. That
is three pixels short: every rotated pipe repeats its first output pixel
four times and then runs three source lines late. A portrait panel driven
in landscape puts each full-screen layer on two pipes, one per mixer, so
the left pipe loses three source lines at the seam in the middle of the
screen and the right pipe shows the last line of its half four times
there. This is the line that made the TB321FU fall back to rotating every
frame with a shader.

Measured on SM8650 (Lenovo TB321FU) by writing back the left mixer output
of a rotated UBWC layer whose pixels encode their source line: preload 4
leaves the output 3 lines late, 5 -> 2, 6 -> 1, 8 -> 1 early, and 7 is
exact, both 1:1 and upscaled 1080p, wherever the source rectangle and the
destination start. The vertical preload has no effect.

Use a horizontal preload of 7 for QSEED4 pipes that rotate.

[ROCKNIX: from https://github.com/enij90/armada-tb321fu/blob/ee94cd659e0cffd4640db8e64ce62f50e28aa37e/packages/kernel/patches/0818-drm-msm-dpu-preload-seven-pixels-in-qseed4-behind-the-inline-rotator.patch]
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c	2026-10-09 21:26:49.249114263 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c	2026-10-09 21:26:49.371042876 +0200
@@ -55,6 +55,15 @@
 #define DPU_QSEED3_DEFAULT_PRELOAD_V 0x3
 #define DPU_QSEED4_DEFAULT_PRELOAD_V 0x2
 #define DPU_QSEED4_DEFAULT_PRELOAD_H 0x4
+/*
+ * With the true inline rotator in front of it, QSEED4 needs three more
+ * pixels of horizontal preload: with the default of 4 every rotated pipe
+ * repeats its first output pixel four times and then runs three source
+ * lines late, which on a panel split across two mixers drops three lines
+ * at the seam. Measured on SM8650 by writing back the mixer output (1:1 and
+ * upscaled): 4 -> 3 lines late, 5 -> 2, 6 -> 1, 7 -> exact, 8 -> 1 early.
+ */
+#define DPU_QSEED4_ROT90_PRELOAD_H 0x7
 
 #define DEFAULT_REFRESH_RATE	60
 
@@ -471,7 +480,9 @@
 		}
 
 		if (pipe_hw->cap->sblk->scaler_blk.version >= 0x3000) {
-			scale_cfg->preload_x[i] = DPU_QSEED4_DEFAULT_PRELOAD_H;
+			scale_cfg->preload_x[i] = inline_rotation ?
+				DPU_QSEED4_ROT90_PRELOAD_H :
+				DPU_QSEED4_DEFAULT_PRELOAD_H;
 			scale_cfg->preload_y[i] = DPU_QSEED4_DEFAULT_PRELOAD_V;
 		} else {
 			scale_cfg->preload_x[i] = DPU_QSEED3_DEFAULT_PRELOAD_H;
